     A*  test26 — the subfile control keywords, written the way real DDS
     A*  writes them: conditioned from the option-indicator columns.
     A*
     A*    SFLCLR    (90)  clear the subfile
     A*    SFLDSP    (91)  display it
     A*    SFLDSPCTL (91)  display the control record
     A*    SFLEND          show More.../Bottom
     A*
     A*  The load-then-display idiom writes the control record TWICE: once
     A*  with *IN90 on to clear, and again after loading with *IN90 off.
     A*  That second write must keep the rows.  It used to wipe them —
     A*  dspf_write cleared the subfile on every control-record write,
     A*  regardless of SFLCLR.
     A          R ROWSFL
     A                                      SFL
     A            ITEM           8A  O  6  2
     A          R ROWCTL
     A                                      SFLCTL(ROWSFL)
     A                                      SFLPAG(5) SFLSIZ(20)
     A  90                                  SFLCLR
     A  91                                  SFLDSP
     A  91                                  SFLDSPCTL
     A                                      SFLEND
     A                                      CF03(03)
     A                                  1  2'Items'
